This product includes work adapted from AgentOps-Bench
(https://github.com/kunwarshivam/agentops-bench), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

What was adapted: the *shapes* of six adversarial prompt-injection delivery
techniques (direct override, authority impersonation, instruction embedded in
an HTML comment within data rows, nested-JSON-value injection, base64-wrapped
payload, and delayed post-processing instruction).

What was not: the payload target and the entire detection mechanism.
AgentOps-Bench's payloads ask a target to leak a system prompt or credentials,
which is checkable only when you control the target and know what is secret.
StressProof runs against strangers' agents as a black box, so it substitutes
its own canary token and detects compliance by literal string matching.

Nine of the fifteen techniques in the original catalogue were deliberately not
carried over: several depend on multi-turn conversation state that StressProof
does not have, and others became duplicates of retained techniques once the
payload was swapped.
